#
# Vulkan games need nothing: the Vulkan loader loads the layer by itself, in every
# application. OpenGL has no equivalent mechanism, so the only way to cover OpenGL
# games without asking the user to configure anything is to be preloaded by the
# session -- which means being preloaded into every process it starts.
#
# What is preloaded is deliberately tiny: a shim with no C++ runtime dependency,
# which does nothing at all until a process presents an OpenGL frame and then
# loads the overlay itself.
#
# $$LIB survives systemd's own variable expansion and reaches the dynamic linker as
# $LIB, which expands to lib or lib32 depending on the architecture of whatever is
# being started -- so one line covers 32-bit and 64-bit games.
#
# To switch the overlay off for a single process, set VOCEM_DISABLE=1.
LD_PRELOAD=${LD_PRELOAD}:@CMAKE_INSTALL_PREFIX@/$$LIB/libvocem_gl_shim.so
